From e90a189c464f3ba02be3fee317a64a483d3d38c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:49:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, voice_input: voice input speaks pt-BR

Voice input (0067, 0085) reads its text through zeo_i18n's t! from
locales/<language>/voice.ftl, in en-US and pt-BR: the button's label,
tooltips and aria label, the consent and download strip, the discarded-
transcript toast, and every notice the voice_input crate raises -- no
microphone, the 2-minute limit, no speech, the CPU check, a missing or
unreadable model, download failures, and the remote transcription's URL,
key, timeout, HTTP and answer errors. The en-US file is the code's English
byte for byte; "<notice>: <reason>" pairs are whole messages with $reason.

The no-speech notice is still compared to decide the outcome logged; both
sides now come from the same function, so they agree in any language.

In the voice group, after 0085.
---

